            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0825" n="711" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg711"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">702.1211/1104: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-27T10:00:00-07:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 27,
                                1922—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:16
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>115. Reference to Oliver Trading Company case, today’s local press published
                    Foreign Office statement to the effect that if the protest stated to have been
                    presented to the Department is not effective Mexican Consulate in New York will
                    be closed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
